---
import SectionHeading from './SectionHeading.astro';
---

<section class="wrap section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <SectionHeading id="about">About</SectionHeading>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I studied Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning at Anurag University and am now in ASU’s M.S. program in Data
      Science, Analytics and Engineering.
    </p>
    <p>
      I usually start a project by deciding how I will know it works. In CodeAtlas that meant hand-written ground truth for
      each fixture and fault injection to score test selection. In the ETL pipeline it meant record counts that must reconcile
      exactly, and in StreamBox a load test that checks the database for duplicates afterward. When a result has limits, such
      as synthetic data or a single machine, I put them next to the number.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .section {
    padding-top: var(--section-gap);
  }

  .prose {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    max-width: var(--width-prose);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }
</style>
